"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[2029],{82029:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"00-vvedenie","title":"Lesson 00. Introduction: Why investing is not the starting point","sourceFingerprint":"061a0c076ec8d55f6603f6074962c9e63e5e6563a6c624cb58a1f59530e8cd9a","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"## Introduction"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"Why investing is not the starting point"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"Most people start learning about money at the wrong end. They open a brokerage account, buy a couple of stocks because everyone else does, and read about crypto. Meanwhile, they pay 50% a year on a credit card and cannot say how much they spend each month. It is rather like fitting a turbocharger to a car that is leaking oil. You gain power, but you will not get far."},{"id":"b004","markdown":"This module explains what to do before investing. It is the unexciting part almost everyone skips, before losing more on the market than they earned there."},{"id":"b005","markdown":"### Why now"},{"id":"b006","markdown":"A few figures from autumn 2026. According to Rosstat, average accrued pay in July was 109 524 RUB. That is before personal income tax and is a mean, not a median, so most people receive less. The Bank of Russia key rate on October 23 was 14%. Annual inflation in September, according to Rosstat, was 6.35%."},{"id":"b007","markdown":"According to the United Credit Bureau, the full cost of credit on credit cards in June was around 50% a year. The average maximum deposit rate at the 10 largest banks, in the central bank’s monitoring for the second ten-day period of October, was 13.06%. Put together, this means a borrowed ruble currently costs 25 to 50% a year, while a deposited ruble earns around 13%."},{"id":"b008","markdown":"You can earn the same salary and live in 2 different economies. In one, you pay interest to the bank every month; in the other, the bank pays you. The distance between them grows with every month."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"Figures at the time of writing"},{"id":"b010","markdown":"Key rate on October 23: 14%. Annual inflation in September 2026: 6.35%. Average maximum deposit rate at the 10 largest banks, second ten-day period of October: 13.06%. The text’s figures are dated to the lesson’s writing. Check current values on the official Bank of Russia website."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"ONE SALARY, TWO ECONOMIES. YOU OWE THE BANK: 25–50% A YEAR, YOU PAY. YOU HAVE A DEPOSIT: BANK ~13% A YEAR, YOU GET PAID. THE GAP GROWS EVERY MONTH."},{"id":"b012","markdown":"### Who this is for"},{"id":"b013","markdown":"If your salary arrives but you cannot explain where it went by month-end. If you have one or several loans and it feels permanent. If you have tried saving but the money was always “needed”. Or if you want to invest but do not know whether you are ready."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"If you have no debt, a six-month cushion and monthly savings, some lessons may seem obvious. Still look at lessons 7, 9 and 10 on fraud, banking and deductions. Those are where people most often lose money through inattention."},{"id":"b015","markdown":"### The order to follow"},{"id":"b016","markdown":"- Lesson 1. What your work is worth and what counts as wealth."},{"id":"b017","markdown":"- Lesson 2. Where the money goes."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"- Lesson 3. How to save without relying on willpower."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"- Lesson 4. Which debts are reasonable and which consume you."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"- Lesson 5. How to escape harmful debt."},{"id":"b021","markdown":"- Lesson 6. The financial cushion."},{"id":"b022","markdown":"- Lesson 7. How to avoid losing everything to fraud."},{"id":"b023","markdown":"- Lesson 8. Inflation, compound interest and what to check before a first investment."},{"id":"b024","markdown":"- Lesson 9. How to make the bank earn less from you and more for you."},{"id":"b025","markdown":"- Lesson 10. Tax deductions."},{"id":"b026","markdown":"There are 2 guides at the end. The first is a 30-day plan with 10 steps you can mark off. The second explains using a credit card without interest, for people who already have no debts and a cushion. Order matters more than any tool. Until expensive debt is repaid and a cushion exists, every investment becomes a lottery. The first setback forces you to sell securities at the worst moment or use the credit card again."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"### How the module works"},{"id":"b028","markdown":"Each lesson takes around 10–15 minutes to read. Each ends with 3 check questions to test whether the main ideas stuck. Figures are dated to October 2026 and come from Rosstat, the Bank of Russia, the Federal Tax Service and credit bureaus. Rates and laws change; the materials will be updated."},{"id":"b029","markdown":"You will not find a list of stocks to buy, schemes to double income, or promises to get rich in a month. This is not a personal investment recommendation; it explains mechanics, and you make the decisions. Before opening the first lesson, answer honestly: how many months could you live if your salary did not arrive tomorrow?"}],"terms":[{"id":"inflyatsiya","term":"Inflation","definition":"A rise in the general price level. In practice: there is more money and the same quantity of goods, so each item costs more. You have not become richer; price tags have simply risen."},{"id":"klyuchevaya-stavka","term":"Key interest rate","definition":"The rate at which the central bank lends to banks. The main monetary-policy tool and the economy’s “price of money”. A higher rate makes loans more expensive and slows inflation."},{"id":"kreditnaya-istoriya","term":"Credit history","definition":"A record of how you repaid loans. A poor or absent history means rejection or a rate above the market. An empty history is worse than a history of repaid loans."},{"id":"nalogovyy-vychet","term":"Tax deduction","definition":"The state refunds part of the tax paid. Up to 260 000 RUB for buying an apartment, 13% for healthcare and education. Real money that people fail to claim because they do not know about it."},{"id":"ndfl","term":"Personal income tax (NDFL)","definition":"Personal income tax. This course’s educational calculations use 13% up to 2.4 million RUB of annual income and 15% for the next band. Since 2025 the main scale has been progressive; special rules apply to other types of income. Check current rates and deduction eligibility with the Federal Tax Service."},{"id":"slozhnyy-protsent","term":"Compound interest","definition":"Interest earning interest. The long-term investor’s main ally: 10 000 RUB invested now for 20 years is worth more than 100 000 RUB invested in 10 years."}],"quizzes":[],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);